# HCL Commerce Integration - Storefront Technical Development Plan
## EDS Storefront Implementation for Add-to-Cart, Mini-Cart & Cart Page

**Date:** March 25, 2026  
**Project:** Mazda AEM Boilerplate Commerce + HCL Commerce Integration  
**Target:** EDS Storefront with HCL Commerce as Commerce Engine  

---

## 📋 Executive Summary

This document outlines the **storefront layer** implementation needed to integrate HCL Commerce with the AEM Boilerplate Commerce EDS storefront. The storefront will:

1. ✅ Call HCL Add-to-Cart API when user clicks "Add to Cart"
2. ✅ Display cart items in mini-cart (header)
3. ✅ Display full cart on dedicated cart page
4. ✅ Handle HCL API responses and errors gracefully
5. ✅ Manage loading states and user feedback
6. ✅ Sync HCL cart data with storefront UI

**Key Assumption:** Integration Agent has already built and deployed the Adobe I/O Runtime actions that wrap HCL APIs and provide:
- Authentication/session management
- Error handling
- CORS headers
- Consistent response formats

---

## 🏗️ Architecture Overview

### Data Flow

```
User Action (PDP)
    ↓
[Add to Cart Button Click]
    ↓
Call Adobe I/O Runtime Action: /api/hcl/cart/add
    ↓
Integration Agent:
  - Check HCL session (WCToken, WCTrustedToken)
  - Call HCL Add-to-Cart API
  - Validate response
  ↓
Return Response:
  {
    "orderId": "764426",
    "orderItem": [{"orderItemId": "6560045"}],
    "cartTotal": "X.XX"
  }
    ↓
[Storefront Updates:]
- Show success message
- Update mini-cart badge
- Update cart page (if open)
```

### File Structure

```
aem-boilerplate-commerce-xcom-ey/
├── blocks/
│   ├── product-details/
│   │   ├── product-details.js          ✏️ MODIFY - Add HCL integration
